.TH TIGRIS\-ACCEPT 8 "7 October 2026" "Tigris 3.5.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
tigris\-accept \- acknowledge a Tigris finding, with a reason and an expiry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tigris\-accept
.I id
.B \-r
.I reason
.RB [ \-u
.IR YYYY\-MM\-DD ]
.RB [ \-m
.IR glob ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.LP
.B tigris\-accept \-l
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.LP
.B tigris\-accept \-d
.I id
.RB [ \-m
.IR glob ]
.RB [ \-f
.IR file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A finding you have looked at and decided to live with can be accepted.
An accepted finding is left out of the text report of
.BR tigris (8)
(the run says how many were) and stays in the JSON report marked
accepted, with the reason and the date. It does not count towards the
exit status. When the date passes, the finding is reported again and
the run warns that the acceptance has expired (acpt001w).
.LP
Without
.BR \-m ,
every message with that id is accepted.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-r " reason"
Why it is accepted. Required when accepting.
.TP
.BI \-u " YYYY\-MM\-DD"
Until when; without it, the acceptance does not expire.
.TP
.BI \-m " glob"
Accept only the messages with that id that match the shell pattern
.IR glob ,
for example
.BR "'docker.service listens on 2283/tcp*'" .
.TP
.B \-l
List the accepted findings.
.TP
.BI \-d " id"
Withdraw an acceptance (with
.BR \-m ,
only the one with that pattern).
.TP
.BI \-f " file"
The acceptance file: by default
.I tigris.accepted
next to the tigerrc
.RI ( ./tigris.accepted
in a source tree,
.I /etc/tiger/tigris.accepted
when installed).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I tigris.accepted
One entry a line, tab-separated: the id, the expiry or \-, the pattern
or \-, and the reason.
.SH EXAMPLES
.RS
.nf
tigris\-accept lin015w \-r "Docker needs IP forwarding"
tigris\-accept sysd001w \-m "docker.service*" \-r "sandboxing tracked in #12" \-u 2027\-01\-31
tigris\-accept \-l
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tigris (8),
.BR tigris\-diff (8)
